    core: `Your Sun and Mercury form a sextile, 60 degrees of productive cooperation between your identity and your mind. Who you are and how you think can support each other without strain. Your conscious direction and your cognitive function are compatible rather than competing. What serves your identity doesn't override your mental processes, and how you think doesn't undermine who you're trying to be. This aspect is less immediate than the conjunction but more flexible. Your mind has some breathing room from your ego, which means you can think about yourself without every thought becoming an identity statement.`,
    behavioral: `Because your identity and your thinking have some distance from each other, you can observe yourself with less defensiveness than the conjunction produces. Self-reflection doesn't automatically trigger ego-protection. You can consider feedback about how you think without it registering as attack on who you are. The sextile means your mental clarity can serve your identity without being fused to it. You think well about your direction, your goals, your sense of self, but you're not so identified with those thoughts that changing your mind feels like losing yourself. This produces intellectual flexibility that others experience as openness rather than rigidity.`,
