    behavioral: `You feel the split between thinking clearly and maintaining identity continuity. Self-reflection can feel threatening because your mind sees things about you that your ego doesn't want to acknowledge. The square creates recurring friction between honest thinking and comfortable self-image. You may override your own mental clarity to protect your sense of self, or you may let your thinking undermine your identity before you've built something solid enough to replace it. The work is learning to hold both: think honestly about yourself without letting those thoughts dissolve who you are before you're ready to change.`,
