    core: `Your Mercury and Venus form a square, 90 degrees of friction between how you think and what you find beautiful. Your cognitive function and your aesthetic sense are calibrated slightly off from each other. What you think wants to express one way. What you find beautiful pulls another. The square means neither force naturally yields. What your mind sees as true may not match what Venus finds appealing, and what you value aesthetically may not hold up under clear thinking.`,
    behavioral: `You feel the tension between thinking clearly and maintaining aesthetic harmony. Your mind wants to pursue truth even when the truth is ugly. Your Venus wants to preserve beauty even when beauty requires ignoring uncomfortable realities. The square creates recurring friction between honest thinking and pleasant communication. You may speak harsh truths that violate relational harmony, or you may smooth your thinking into pleasant forms that aren't actually accurate. The work is learning to hold both: think clearly without weaponizing the truth, and value beauty without using it to avoid what's real.`,
    friendship: `Friends may experience you as someone whose communication style fluctuates between honest directness and careful pleasantness. Sometimes clarity matters more. Sometimes harmony matters more.`,
